---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ExamResizer from '../components/ExamResizer.astro';
import SEOContent from '../components/SEOContent.astro';

const SEO_TITLE = "NEET Photo, Signature & Fingerprint Resizer";
const SEO_DESC = "Free NEET image resizer. Instantly crop and compress your NEET photo, signature, and fingerprint (10KB-200KB) to exact NTA guidelines. Better than Exammint.";
---

<Layout title={SEO_TITLE} description={SEO_DESC} showMesh={true}>
  <!-- Tool Section -->
  <section class="relative z-20 pt-16 container-stripe">
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 32px;">
      <div style="display: inline-block; padding: 6px 16px; background: rgba(200, 241, 53, 0.1); border: 1px solid rgba(200, 241, 53, 0.3); border-radius: 100px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-lime); margin-bottom: 16px;">
        NTA EXAM READY
      </div>
      <h1 style="font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.25rem); line-height: 1.05; margin: 0 0 16px; letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        NEET <span style="color: var(--color-lime);">Photo Resizer</span>
      </h1>
      <p style="font-size: 1.0625rem; color: var(--color-ink-2); max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto; line-height: 1.65;">
        Format your Passport Photo, Postcard Photo, Signature, and Thumb Impression instantly for the NTA NEET application portal.
      </p>
    </div>
    
    <ExamResizer defaultExam="neet" defaultType="photo" allowMultiple={true} />
  </section>

  <!-- SEO Content Section -->
  <SEOContent 
    targetKB="180KB" 
    customTitle="Ultimate Guide to NEET Application Photo Requirements 2026"
    uniqueContent={`
      <p class="seo-p">
        The National Eligibility cum Entrance Test (NEET UG) is India's most competitive medical entrance exam. While Class 12 students spend months preparing for biology, physics, and chemistry, many find themselves struggling with a surprising obstacle: the <strong>NEET photo upload</strong> process. The National Testing Agency (NTA) has extremely strict guidelines for how your documents must be formatted. A single mistake in your <strong>NEET ug photo size</strong> can lead to your application being temporarily withheld or even rejected. Using our dedicated <strong>NEET photo resize</strong> tool ensures your passport photos, postcard photos, and signatures are instantly formatted to NTA's exact specifications, right in your browser.
      </p>

      <h3 class="seo-h3" style="margin-top: 40px;">EXACT NEET UG 2026 Photo Requirements</h3>
      <p class="seo-p">
        To successfully submit your application for 2026, you must prepare four distinct image files. Every file must be in JPG or JPEG format. Here is the definitive breakdown:
      </p>
      <ul class="seo-list" style="margin-bottom: 32px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;">
        <li style="display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start;">
          <strong style="color: var(--color-lime); min-width: 150px;">Passport Photo:</strong>
          <span class="seo-p-small">Must be between 10 KB and 200 KB. The background must be plain white. Your face should cover 80% of the frame (ears clearly visible). Name and date of taking the photograph must be printed at the bottom. No masks, caps, or dark glasses.</span>
        </li>
        <li style="display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start;">
          <strong style="color: var(--color-lime); min-width: 150px;">Postcard Photo:</strong>
          <span class="seo-p-small">Dimensions must be exactly 4x6 inches. File size between 10 KB and 200 KB. This is a larger version of your passport photo and must have the same white background and 80% face coverage. This will be checked at the exam center.</span>
        </li>
        <li style="display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start;">
          <strong style="color: var(--color-lime); min-width: 150px;">Signature:</strong>
          <span class="seo-p-small">Size must be strictly between 4 KB and 30 KB. You must sign with a black pen on a white sheet of paper. Do not sign in ALL CAPS, as this will be instantly rejected.</span>
        </li>
        <li style="display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start;">
          <strong style="color: var(--color-lime); min-width: 150px;">Thumb Impression:</strong>
          <span class="seo-p-small">Left and Right hand fingers and thumb impressions are required. Size must be between 10 KB and 200 KB. Use blue or black ink on a white paper. Ensure it is not smudged.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="seo-h3">Photo Booth vs. Smartphone: Which Works Better for NEET?</h3>
      <p class="seo-p">
        Many Class 12 students wonder if they need a professional studio for their <strong>NEET application photo requirements 2026</strong>. While a professional photo booth ensures perfect lighting and a pure white background, modern smartphones are more than capable—if you follow a few tips. If using a smartphone, stand 2 feet in front of a well-lit white wall during daylight. Have a family member take the photo from chest height using the rear camera (never use a selfie!). Once you have the raw photo, you can use our <strong>NEET photo resize</strong> tool to crop it to the correct proportions, apply a white background filter if needed, and compress it to the NTA's rigid 10KB-200KB limit. 
      </p>

      <h3 class="seo-h3">NTA NEET Portal Photo Upload Troubleshooting</h3>
      <p class="seo-p">
        The NTA portal is notorious for rejecting uploads without clear error messages. If your <strong>NEET photo upload</strong> is failing, check these common culprits:
      </p>
      <ul class="seo-list" style="margin-bottom: 32px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;">
        <li style="display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start;">
           <span class="seo-step-num" style="width: 24px; height: 24px; font-size: 12px; line-height: 24px; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; border-radius: 50%; border: 1px solid var(--color-border-mid); color: var(--color-lime);">1</span>
           <span class="seo-p-small"><strong>File Format Issues:</strong> Ensure your file ends in .jpg or .jpeg. PNG or PDF files will trigger an error.</span>
        </li>
        <li style="display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start;">
           <span class="seo-step-num" style="width: 24px; height: 24px; font-size: 12px; line-height: 24px; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; border-radius: 50%; border: 1px solid var(--color-border-mid); color: var(--color-lime);">2</span>
           <span class="seo-p-small"><strong>Size Boundaries:</strong> If your signature is 30.5 KB, the portal will reject it. Always aim for the middle of the range (e.g., 15 KB for signatures, 100 KB for photos).</span>
        </li>
        <li style="display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start;">
           <span class="seo-step-num" style="width: 24px; height: 24px; font-size: 12px; line-height: 24px; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; border-radius: 50%; border: 1px solid var(--color-border-mid); color: var(--color-lime);">3</span>
           <span class="seo-p-small"><strong>Browser Cache:</strong> The NTA portal sometimes hangs on slow internet. Clear your cache or try incognito mode if the upload button becomes unresponsive.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="seo-h3">What Happens if Your NEET Photo is Rejected? (The Re-correction Window)</h3>
      <p class="seo-p">
        Don't panic if you realize you made a mistake after submitting. The NTA usually opens a "Correction Window" a few weeks after the application deadline closes. During this period, candidates who received an email or SMS regarding an "Image Discrepancy" can log back into the portal and re-upload their documents. However, this is a stressful process and server traffic during the correction window is heavily congested. It is always better to get your <strong>NEET ug photo size</strong> and format right on the first attempt using a dedicated resizing utility.
      </p>
    `}
    customFaqs={[
      {
        q: "What is the difference between passport and postcard size for NEET?",
        a: "A passport size photo is the standard small photograph (approx 3.5cm x 4.5cm) used for the main application form. A postcard size photo is larger (4x6 inches). Both must have the same image (your face, white background, name, and date) and be sized between 10 KB to 200 KB. You must physically carry the postcard size photo to the exam center."
      },
      {
        q: "Does my NEET photo need my name and date printed on it?",
        a: "Yes. According to the NTA guidelines, the photograph must have the candidate's name and the date the photograph was taken printed clearly at the bottom."
      },
      {
        q: "Can I use a blue background for my NEET application photo?",
        a: "No. The NTA explicitly requires a plain white background for both the passport and postcard size photographs. Using a blue or colored background is a common reason for image rejection."
      },
      {
        q: "Why is my signature file being rejected by the NTA portal?",
        a: "Signatures are rejected most commonly for three reasons: the file size is outside the strict 4 KB to 30 KB limit, the signature is in ALL CAPS (which is prohibited), or it was signed with a color other than black on white paper."
      },
      {
        q: "Should I wear spectacles in my NEET photograph?",
        a: "You may wear spectacles only if you use them regularly. However, you must ensure there is no flash reflection or glare on the lenses, and dark glasses/sunglasses are strictly prohibited."
      }
    ]}
  />
</Layout>
